{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/314211-new-to-scion-and-st-a-few-questions","id":314211,"title":"New to Scion and ST, a few questions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-16T21:55:03-08:00","id":314211,"title":"New to Scion and ST, a few questions.","content":"OK so I've gone through basically the whole Hero book so that I understand the basics before going through all the other books. I pretty much understand all the mechanics, except for two things.<br /> <br /> Firstly is damage (pretty important). I understand the calculations: raw damage is weapon + character strength + threshold successes +1, roll that many die, subtract the target's soak from those successes, and that's the damage the target takes. But what is the damage applied to? I saw the levels, but surely it doesn't directly damage those or else the characters would die incredibly easily, right? Or am I just overestimating how much damage a single attack roll does?<br /> <br /> The second question is about time, mainly stuff that involves minutes, hours, and days. Is all of that up to the ST's discretion, or is there a specific mechanical system that dictates how time passes (other than discussing ticks, sessions, scenes, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4311-sparky-young-upstart","name":"Sparky Young Upstart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T22:35:17-08:00","id":314270,"title":"","content":"Unless you're throwing a massively over-powered creature (say one with Epic Dex or Strength), you tend not to take a lot of damage. Particularly if characters know combat is coming, they'd likely be wearing some kind of armour or whatever (thick coats is favourite in my experience). And yes, each success left after soak is one level of damage. (Bear in mind each dice has a roughly 30% change of success, which means on 10 dice you'd expect 3-ish successes. One soak reduces that to 2).<br /> <br /> The second, not usually any guideline. Ticks <i>tend</i> to be roughly a second or two each, and a scene is supposed to roughly correspond to an hour. Sessions can cover nearly any length of time, but in my experience tend to cover a day or three. Of course, obviously these suggestions can and do vary hugely depending on context.<br /> <br /> If you've uncomfortable with the mechanics, get someone to make up a character (or use one of the samples) and run through a combat.<br /> <br /> Because you say you're new to STing, best recommendation I can give: listen to your players, and don't get so in love with your carefully crafted story that you can't adapt. Oh, and if you're looking to creep out your players, don't just gross them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T17:07:24-08:00","id":314943,"title":"","content":"OK, thanks. That helps a lot. One other question: Is it possible for a Scion to obtain more relics or upgrade the relics they have by spending XP in order to make them stronger or access more purviews during the course of the story? I didn't see anything on the advancement table in Hero, but since I've yet to get a hold of the Demigod or God books I know there might be stuff about new relics in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4311-sparky-young-upstart","name":"Sparky Young Upstart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T17:26:23-08:00","id":314960,"title":"","content":"Technically not. Relics are set, and are meant to be acquired through play. For example, if you look at the entries under Antagonist, you'll note a lot of them have bits that count as Relics for the purposes of accessing Purviews, and usually have some minor bonuses. So if your Scions are killing titanspawn on a semi-regular basis, they'd likely get in the habit of eyeballing the remains/loot, seeing if any of it is a Relic.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's nothing stopping you house-ruling such a thing. A Scion can bond more closely with their Relic, which allows them to unlock more of its power. Not supported by rules I think, but interesting nonetheless. Just make it sufficiently epic and difficult RP-wise (like the Scion has to go on a dreamwalk into their own souls and confront their fears in order to access the Fertility Purview through this Harpy claw).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T17:53:43-08:00","id":314969,"title":"","content":"In the rules, the only way to power-up your Relics or other Birthrights is by adding more dots to them at the Demigod or God boosts. That's also the only way, mechanically, to acquire more of them.<br /> <br /> However, Birthrights are basically &quot;Backgrounds&quot; as described in all other White Wolf systems, and there has always been the option (generally the <i>singular</i> option) of increasing them or gaining them through play. So if you want to buff your Relic, go on a Heroic Quest. Or douse it in the blood of a giant, or whatever. It doesn't cost anything except time and effort. It's kinda a crappy system, since everything <i>else</i> requires XP... but there ya go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T13:43:01-08:00","id":320144,"title":"","content":"I would also consider all the smith gods and friendly titanspawn/creatures that have relic building abilities another possibility. The Dwarves and good Tengu immediately come to mind. A simple favor or a favor or I'm sure the Storyteller can come up with some task/mission. People like Hephaestus aren't necessarily some stranger. They could be uncles to your character or slightly more distant relatives but relatives nonetheless. The various creature races would also provide role playing opportunities beyond the 'do the mission I buff your relic battleaxe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T09:22:32-08:00","id":320797,"title":"","content":"Trophies, maybe, but probably not Relics. Relics are bound into your Legend and come from mom or dad (and it looks like they should require a high level Magic Boon, even for deities that don't have Magic...). Trophies are things you pick up along the way. Certain values of 'picking up' = commissioned works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}